1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,599
The HTTPS module can redirect visitors from HTTP to HTTPS, and can tell

2
00:00:06,599 --> 00:00:09,144
browsers to keep using HTTPS.

3
00:00:09,144 --> 00:00:13,871
In this video, you turn the module on, set it up, and learn

4
00:00:13,871 --> 00:00:15,980
what each setting does.

5
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:26,720
Over plain HTTP, the data between a browser and your site travels as readable text.

6
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:32,170
HTTPS encrypts that connection, so the data cannot be read along the way.

7
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,519
When Require HTTPS is on, a request that arrives over HTTP receives a redirect.

8
00:00:39,519 --> 00:00:46,740
The browser follows it to the HTTPS address, and the rest of the exchange is encrypted.

9
00:00:47,490 --> 00:00:50,562
The settings page has four settings.

10
00:00:50,562 --> 00:00:56,997
Require HTTPS turns the redirect on, and HSTS mode controls a header for browsers.

11
00:00:56,997 --> 00:01:04,530
Require HTTPS Permanent chooses a permanent redirect, and SSL Port names the port to redirect to.

12
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:12,889
HTTP Strict Transport Security, or HSTS, is a header that tells browsers to use HTTPS only.

13
00:01:12,889 --> 00:01:18,771
The module sends it with a lifetime of 365 days, subdomains included.

14
00:01:18,771 --> 00:01:21,909
HSTS mode decides when it is sent:

15
00:01:21,909 --> 00:01:26,380
never, in every environment, or only in Production.

16
00:01:27,130 --> 00:01:32,147
The settings can be changed only when the page is opened over HTTPS.

17
00:01:32,147 --> 00:01:37,909
Over plain HTTP, a message says that changing HTTPS-only settings over HTTP has

18
00:01:37,909 --> 00:01:42,180
been prevented, and the changes you save are not applied.

19
00:01:46,412 --> 00:01:48,579
Let's turn the module on.

20
00:01:48,579 --> 00:01:52,842
Open Tools, Features, and type HTTPS in the search box.

21
00:01:53,299 --> 00:01:58,989
HTTPS is listed in the Security category, with a description of what the module does.

22
00:01:59,453 --> 00:02:00,816
Select Enable.

23
00:02:00,816 --> 00:02:02,520
A message confirms:

24
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:04,973
The feature HTTPS was enabled.

25
00:02:09,203 --> 00:02:11,882
Open Settings, Security, HTTPS.

26
00:02:11,882 --> 00:02:18,253
A warning at the top says the website might be restarted upon saving the settings.

27
00:02:18,713 --> 00:02:21,099
Let's select Require HTTPS.

28
00:02:21,099 --> 00:02:26,523
It applies to all requests, so once the settings are saved, a request

29
00:02:26,523 --> 00:02:30,283
that arrives over HTTP is redirected to HTTPS.

30
00:02:30,735 --> 00:02:32,432
Below it is HSTS mode.

31
00:02:32,432 --> 00:02:37,644
The notice under the drop-down list warns that browsers may stop connecting over

32
00:02:37,644 --> 00:02:42,130
HTTP after receiving the header, if HTTPS later becomes unavailable.

33
00:02:42,130 --> 00:02:47,585
Let's choose the option From environment, enabled in Production, disabled otherwise.

34
00:02:48,042 --> 00:02:53,809
Require HTTPS Permanent switches the redirect from a temporary one to a permanent one.

35
00:02:53,809 --> 00:02:58,072
Let's leave it unselected, which keeps the temporary redirect.

36
00:02:58,545 --> 00:03:00,955
SSL Port is the port to redirect to.

37
00:03:00,955 --> 00:03:03,825
Here it already shows the port of this page.

38
00:03:03,825 --> 00:03:07,785
Leave it empty to let the site try to work the port out itself.

39
00:03:08,241 --> 00:03:09,351
Select Save.

40
00:03:09,351 --> 00:03:10,892
A message confirms:

41
00:03:10,892 --> 00:03:13,421
Site settings updated successfully.

42
00:03:13,881 --> 00:03:16,624
The page shows the saved settings:

43
00:03:16,624 --> 00:03:22,181
Require HTTPS is selected, and HSTS mode shows the From environment option.

44
00:03:26,381 --> 00:03:33,057
Once the saved settings are applied, a request that arrives over HTTP is redirected to HTTPS.

45
00:03:33,057 --> 00:03:37,441
This applies to every page of the site, not only the admin.

46
00:03:38,191 --> 00:03:42,305
The settings belong to the tenant, so each tenant of a site has

47
00:03:42,305 --> 00:03:44,034
its own HTTPS settings.

48
00:03:44,034 --> 00:03:48,625
Saving reloads the tenant, which the warning on the page describes as a

49
00:03:48,625 --> 00:03:50,891
possible restart of the website.

50
00:03:51,641 --> 00:03:56,308
If a load balancer handles HTTPS and passes plain HTTP to the site,

51
00:03:56,308 --> 00:04:01,231
the site sees HTTP requests, and the page ignores the changes you save.

52
00:04:01,231 --> 00:04:05,963
The Reverse Proxy settings can forward the protocol the client used.

53
00:04:05,963 --> 00:04:08,201
A separate video covers them.

54
00:04:10,201 --> 00:04:12,342
That's the HTTPS module:

55
00:04:12,342 --> 00:04:17,482
a redirect from HTTP to HTTPS, a choice of redirect type and port,

56
00:04:17,482 --> 00:04:19,124
and an HSTS mode.

57
00:04:19,124 --> 00:04:20,981
Thanks for watching.

